<title>SRI LANKA: Sri Lanka 1996 wheat imports fall after price rise.</title>
<headline>Sri Lanka 1996 wheat imports fall after price rise.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1997-05-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sri Lanka's wheat imports fell by 14 percent to 913,000 tonnes last year from just over one million tonnes in 1995, according to provisional figures in the Central Bank's annual report.</p>
<p>The fall in wheat imports was a result of a drop in domestic demand because of a rise in administered flour prices after the reduction of the wheat subsidy, said the report released on Wednesday.</p>
</text>
